  "reason": "Evidence: The best config so far is config_041 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.7250 acc. All 7 completed experiments used multiprofile; the singleprofile dimension is entirely untested. Within multiprofile, transformer > avgpool and weighted > concat, and scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l is the dominant encoder pair. Question: config_004 tests whether the singleprofile architecture (no aggregation, direct fusion) with the proven best encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) and best fusion (weighted) can match or exceed the multiprofile + transformer pipeline. Rationale: With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, I need to either confirm the current best or find a competitive alternative. Singleprofile is the largest unexplored axis, and if it performs comparably or better, it opens a new exploitation direction for the final 2 runs. Choosing weighted over concat (config_002) is consistent with the small but consistent edge weighted has shown (0.7250 vs 0.7207)."
}

